      "writtenOn": "2017-11-07T10:41:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A clear example of slow PNG encoding is when image is not UI (for example, a game), and contains lots of unpredictable colors, which makes PNG encoding slow. \nTried on a Note8 (QHD+) with the game TempleRun2.\n$ time ./screencap_jpg -p test; ls -al test           \n    0m05.01s real     0m04.81s user     0m00.14s system\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 root root 5227566 2017-11-07 10:09 test\n$ time ./screencap_jpg -j test; ls -al test           \n    0m00.86s real     0m00.66s user     0m00.15s system\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 root root 510783 2017-11-07 10:09 test\n\nAnd since PNG image sizes are big, file transfers are also slow.\nGiving the option to encode at lower res, or faster encoders is very useful for some use cases.",
      "parentUuid": "1cf80578_46de4485",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 9,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "a4d44415c905be192c0e62d0e86a7163abb170c5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
